    "committer": "EllisPatrick <ellis.patrick@sydney.edu.au>",
    "message": "1.99.21: the cell method's image-by-image loop in the shared C++ core; imageInfo and tableKey; writeCellStore() and a store example in the vignette\n\n- src/core/src/stream.cpp, spicyglm/stream.hpp (new, shared with spicyr): batch_totals(), rows_totals() and\n  stream_totals() run each image in a Dataset of its own, the images handed out to threads in turn; scan_codes(),\n  constant_within(), rows_differing(), rows_of_images() and first_appearance_codes() are the passes over the codes.\n  src/glm_bindings.cpp keeps thin wrappers (cell_block_scan replaces cell_layout). Results identical: 222/236\n  test expectations, memref 8 of 8 identical(), the 100M store identical() to the data.frame run (1 and 8 cores),\n  100M and 1B results identical() to 1.99.20.\n- spicy(): `table` is renamed `tableKey`; new `imageInfo` (data.frame or the name of a table of the store or\n  SpatialData object) for condition, subject, covariates or a Surv outcome missing from the cell table, for\n  data.frames and stores (survival from a store now works). Errors for missing and unknown images.\n- writeCellStore() (exported) writes cells as a SpatialData store with anndataR; spatialdataR and anndataR in\n  Suggests. Vignette: \"Very large data sets: SpatialData stores\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TfsjwkbDbHkX4kJZNe4ER4\n",
    "time": 1792074056
  },
